{"name":"Puff Pastry Yellow","hex":"#fccf8b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"puff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sharp exhalation of a small amount of breath through the mouth.","The ability to breathe easily while exerting oneself."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit smoke, gas, etc., in puffs.","To pant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff"},{"term":"pastry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A baked food item  made from flour and fat pastes such as pie crust; also tarts, bear claws, napoleons, puff pastries, etc.","The food group formed by the various kinds of pastries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastry"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Puff pastry","blocks":[{"text":"Puff pastry, also known as pâte feuilletée, is a light, flaky pastry, its base dough composed of wheat flour and water. Butter or other solid fat is then layered into the dough. The dough is repeatedly rolled and folded, rested, re-rolled and folded, encasing solid butter between each resulting layer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Pate_feuilletee_2.jpg/330px-Pate_feuilletee_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puff_pastry"},{"title":"Pastry","blocks":[{"text":"Pastry is various unleavened doughs, often enriched with fat or eggs. The dough may be called pastry dough. Common pastry dishes include börek, pies, tarts, and turnovers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Making_puff_pastry_%28butter_and_Water_dough_%29_5.jpg/330px-Making_puff_pastry_%28butter_and_Water_dough_%29_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pastry"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Empanadas_de_At%C3%BAn-2009.jpg/500px-Empanadas_de_At%C3%BAn-2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Empanadas_de_At%C3%BAn-2009.jpg/1280px-Empanadas_de_At%C3%BAn-2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Empanadas_de_At%C3%BAn-2009.jpg/500px-Empanadas_de_At%C3%BAn